{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Why do you cry out to me.</b> According to the plain sense, Moses was certain that they would be delivered, for HaShem had already said to him, 'ואכבדה בפרעה' etc. Rather, He says this concerning Israel, for they were crying out — that is, why are you crying out? For in every place He speaks with Moses on behalf of Israel. 'Speak to the children of Israel and they shall journey on' — behold, you have already said to them in My name, 'YHWH will fight for you'; they were certain that He would not allow me to defeat them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:46.701732911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}